  "details": "So my story is like this: if I hang out in public worlds, then most of the time these worlds are cross-platform. For this reason I looked up several Quest-compatible public avatars to wear if I notice a lot of Quest users in the lobby. The problem here is that on that platform by default performance rank blocking works as described here:\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/avatar-performance-ranking-system#section-quest-limits\nSince I can't see Quest-specific performance rating for avatar that I have on right now, Quest users most of the time need to manually show my avatar if it's rated Very Poor. Unfortunately quite often Quest versions of avatars are just PC versions with swapped shaders, which 100% of time results in Very Poor rating.\nMy suggestion here is to for example add a 2nd page to Avatar Stats popup where you can see all information specific to the version that only Quest users can see, or at least display performance ranking icon somewhere for it.",
